      "The reasons were physical. In a longer chain, the frequencies of the vibrational modes crowd together, and it becomes harder to address a single mode without exciting others. The gate speed slows down, and heating of the motion degrades the fidelity. The NIST and Michigan authors, with long experience in ion manipulation, asked how to avoid the limit by using the capability to move ions.",
