    technicalAbstract: "The paper proves that quantum computation can be made fault tolerant: for any quantum circuit and any desired accuracy, there is a simulating circuit on noisy gates that computes the same function, with polylogarithmic overhead, provided the noise rate per gate is below a constant threshold. The proof is based on concatenated codes and a recursive construction of fault-tolerant gadgets, and it applies to a model of local noise.",
