      "Only after the heralding signal arrives at the stations does the measurement begin, which makes the test event-ready, and thus the sample is not biased by the failed attempts. At each station, a random number generator selects a measurement setting, and the spin is read out, in a time shorter than the light travel time between the stations, so no signal could have told one station the setting at the other before it finished.",
      "The experiment ran for about 220 hours, with 245 valid trials in total. For each trial the correlations between the two outcomes were computed for the four combinations of settings, and the CHSH quantity was found to be 2.42 with an uncertainty of 0.20, above the local limit of 2. A statistical test, with a model-independent analysis of the run, gave a p-value of about 0.039 against the local hidden variable hypothesis.",
